# The JAXA 30P30N three-element section, meshed the way its own reference mesh is:
# a structured near-wall ribbon on every surface, unstructured triangles outside.
#
# WHAT THIS IS MATCHED AGAINST, and the numbers it is held to, are in
# docs/research/jaxa-30p30n-reference-mesh.md -- which measured the reference
# project file itself (20 structured ribbons of ~1.5% chord, 206,370 quads;
# 1,011,462 triangles outside them; 1.22 M cells over x in [-5,4], y in [-5,3]).
#
# THE RIBBON DEPTH, and what used to cap it. 0.0038 chord here is a quarter of
# the reference's 0.015. It used to be forced: two fronts growing into each
# other aborted the whole run, and this file recorded it as "builds at 0.0038,
# fails at 0.0042 with Critical proximity detected after retreat".
#
# THAT CAP IS GONE. Two geometries' fronts that meet now FREEZE the nodes
# involved and the layer tapers to zero there, which is what the published
# practice does when a front cannot advance -- it stops that node, not the run
# (docs/research/meshing-the-cove-and-the-trailing-edges.md; gated by
# tools/PreProcessor/tests/test_bl_front_meeting.py). Re-measured 2026-11-02:
# this section builds at BL_LAYERS 120, i.e. 0.0089 chord, exit 0, with one
# warning naming the slot at (0.8767, 0.0249) where the taper starts -- at
# LAYER 92 of 123. This comment said "layer 9" until 2026-11-02,
# a dropped digit, and the conclusion drawn from it ("so that stretch was
# always going to be thin") was the wrong one: 92 layers is 0.0064 chord of
# ribbon on each side, which is two halves of the 1.27% slot, so the two
# fronts stop where they MEET and not where they fail. Re-run to check it:
# the same warning at BL_LAYERS 160 also says layer 92, as it must, because
# the layer heights do not depend on how many were asked for.
# That run cost 1,214,780 cells BEFORE the far-field change below and
# 1,832,326 after it (re-run 2026-11-02). Both are kept: the ribbon is the
# same in each and only the fill around it differs, which is the point.
#
# 160 LAYERS USED TO FAIL, and does not any more (#179, 2026-11-03). It was
# exit 5, the slat (Geometry 0) self-intersecting in its own final front at
# (-0.0280, -0.0950) -- 0.0138 from the wall where 163 layers reach 0.0137, on
# the medial axis between the slat's concave COVE and the fan around its sharp
# tip at (-0.0267, -0.1088), an 11 deg included angle. The final ring now
# TAPERS where it crosses instead of throwing away the mesh it has built:
# 160 layers gives 2,017,055 cells and 180 gives 2,033,547, both exit 0.
#
# SO THE REFERENCE'S OWN RIBBON DEPTH IS REACHABLE: 180 layers is 0.0150
# chord, which is target 1 of the research note. BL_LAYERS stays at 60 anyway
# -- 2.03 M cells against the reference's 1.22 M is not a trade this case
# wants, and the depth has been a choice rather than a cap since 178b2c1.
# What is NOT clean at 180: four triangles of about -5e-10 at the slat fold,
# which the mesher's own inverted count (0) does not see and a signed area
# does. Named in .claude/rules/mesher.md's blind spots.
#
# BL_LAYERS stays at 60 so this shipped case keeps its size and its cost. The
# depth is now a choice rather than a cap; raise it if you want the ribbon.
#
# THE FAR FIELD AND THE WAKE, changed 2026-11-02 and measured against the
# reference's own table rather than against the eye. Six runs, all BL_LAYERS
# 60, cell sizes as median EDGE length (this file's measurements used to be
# sqrt(area), which is 0.658x an edge on an equilateral triangle -- both are
# stated wherever one is):
#
#   cap     rate   wake seed        cells       wake edge   edge at 3-5 chords
#   1.0     0.014  none             790,353     0.0054      0.0508
#   1.0     0.014  0.0022 / 0.65    790,819     0.0054      0.0508   <- INERT
#   0.0152  0.014  none           1,333,330     0.0060      0.0152
#   0.0152  0.014  0.0022 / 0.65  1,417,656     0.0036      0.0152   <- SHIPPED
#   0.0152  0.014  trimmed to 1.4 1,341,678     0.0046      0.0152
#   0.05    0.05   0.0022 / 2.39    589,652     0.0036      0.0500
#   reference                     ~1,220,000    0.00223*    0.0152
#   (* the reference's finest level is a BOX ending at x = 1.213, not a band
#    running downstream; past x = 1.4 it is at the 0.0152 far field.)
#
# ROWS 2 AND 3 ARE THE CONTROLS THAT EARN THE PAIRING. The seed alone, under
# the dead cap, moved 466 cells of 790,353 and left the wake where it was. The
# cap alone left the wake at 0.0060. Only together do they reach 0.0036: the
# cap is what gives the seed's Threshold a SizeMax low enough to win the Min(),
# and the seed is what puts the wake below the cap. Neither is half the fix.
#
# The shipped row costs 1.8x the old one and that is the cap, not the seed:
# trimming the seed to the reference's own extent saves 5%, because 0.0152 over
# x in [-5,4] y in [-5,3] is 598,000 cells beyond one chord however the wake is
# drawn. Against the reference's own 1.22 M the shipped row is +16% and the
# trimmed one +10%; an earlier draft of this comment put the SHIPPED row
# within 10%, which is the trimmed row's figure and not this one's.
#
# THE LAST ROW IS THE CHEAP ALTERNATIVE and it is not a worse mesh everywhere:
# it resolves the wake exactly as well (0.0036) for 590 k cells -- FEWER than
# the 790 k this case used to cost -- by declining to pay for the reference's
# far field. Take it by setting FARFIELD_MESH_SIZE 0.05, FARFIELD_GROWTH_RATE
# 0.05 and the seed radius to 2.39, which is what keeps the wake gradient at
# the same 0.02 per unit when the cap moves. It is not the default only because
# this file's stated job is to be matched against the reference.
LENGTH_UNIT custom
LENGTH_UNIT_METRES 0.4572          # the stowed chord, so lengths here are chords
MESH_MODE 0

DOMAIN_X_MIN -5.0
DOMAIN_X_MAX  4.0
DOMAIN_Y_MIN -5.0
DOMAIN_Y_MAX  3.0

SURFACE_MESH_SIZE 0.004
AUTO_SURFACE_SIZE 1
# 0.0152 is the reference's OWN far-field edge length, which it holds CONSTANT
# all the way to 5 chords -- 754,820 of its 1.22 M cells are there. This key is
# a Min() CAP, never a target (.claude/rules/mesher.md), and it sat at the 1.0
# default until 2026-11-02 while the ramp below was derived. A cap the ramp
# never reaches is not a loose cap, it is NO cap: the size went on climbing to
# 0.0984 and the far field came out at 0.0508 edge, 3.3x COARSER than the
# reference it is matched against. Measured here with it live: active over
# 59.9% of the domain, and d = 1..5 chords all read 0.0152 exactly.
FARFIELD_MESH_SIZE 0.0152
# 0.014 is derived, not tuned by eye: the size field is LINEAR in the distance
# from the boundary-layer front, so this rate is what puts ~0.0034 chord at the
# distance where the reference's near field reads ~0.0039.
FARFIELD_GROWTH_RATE 0.014

# THE WAKE. The size field above is a function of wall distance ALONE, so it
# can only draw circles: before this line the mesh had an isotropic halo and
# nothing downstream, where the reference puts its FINEST level (0.00223 over
# the slot and the flap's wake). That is O5 in
# docs/research/jaxa-30p30n-reference-mesh.md -- "no law in distance from the
# wall can produce it" -- and a refinement seed is how this repo expresses it.
#
# A seed's RADIUS IS AN INVERSE GRADIENT, not a box size: the Threshold runs
# from `size` at the seed to FARFIELD_MESH_SIZE at `radius`, so this pair asks
# for (0.0152 - 0.0022) / 0.65 = 0.02 per unit length.
#
# WHICH IS WHY THE TWO LINES BELONG TOGETHER, measured as a control on
# 2026-11-02: this exact seed added while the cap was still 1.0 asked for 1.53
# per unit, lost the Min() to the wall ramp at the first cell, and changed the
# mesh by 466 cells out of 790,353 -- INERT. The cap is what makes the seed do
# anything.
SEED_FILE examples/geometries/30p30n_wake_seed.dat 0.0022 0.65 source

# 60 layers, first cell 5.4e-5 chord, growth 1.005 -> 0.0038 total. The near
# uniform normal spacing is the reference's own: its ribbons run 0.2 to 2.2 in
# last-over-first interval, not the 50-100x of a stretched layer.
BL_INITIAL_THICKNESS 0.00005446
BL_GROWTH_RATE 1.005
BL_LAYERS 60

BL_CONVEX_METHOD 0
BL_FAN_NODES 5
BL_AUTO_FAN_NODES 1
BL_FAN_ANGLE_THRESHOLD 60.0
BL_CONCAVE_METHOD 5
BL_CONCAVE_ANGLE_THRESHOLD 120.0
BL_TRANSITION_LAYERS 3
BL_TRANSITION_GROWTH_RATE 1.15
BL_TRANSITION_BUFFER 2.0
GMSH_ALGORITHM 6
GMSH_OPTIMIZE 1
ENABLE_COLLISION_DETECTION 1

EXPORT_VTK 1
EXPORT_STARCD 1
BC_GEOM wall
BC_XMIN inlet
BC_XMAX outlet
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/30p30n_jaxa_slat.dat
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/30p30n_jaxa_main.dat
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/30p30n_jaxa_flap.dat
OUTPUT_FILENAME results/meshes/hybrid_30p30n/mesh_hybrid_30p30n.vtk
